%description:
Tests the FIN of a segment of old data (RFC 9293: SEG.LEN counts the SYN and the
FIN). The client sends 100 bytes and closes at t=1.1 s; the tester deletes its
FIN and the ACK of the server. After the RTO, the client sends the 100 bytes
again with the FIN. The server already has the data, but the FIN lies at
RCV.NXT, so the segment is acceptable: the server takes the FIN and
acknowledges 102. Master measured only the data, refused the segment, and the
FIN waited for one more RTO.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 100"
*.cli_app.tClose=1.1s
*.tcptester.script="A4 delete; B2 delete"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[1.001 A003] A.1000 > B.2000: A 1:101(100) ack 501 win 16384 
cli_tcp: ESTABLISHED --> FIN_WAIT_1  (on CLOSE)
[1.101 A004] A.1000 > B.2000: A F ack 501 win 16384 # deleting
[1.203 B002] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 101 win 16384 # deleting
[4.001 A005] A.1000 > B.2000: A F 1:101(100) ack 501 win 16384 
srv_tcp: ESTABLISHED --> CLOSE_WAIT  (on RCV_FIN)
[4.003 B003] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 102 win 16384 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
